## Problem

# llama-patch (github.com/PromptExecution/llama-patch) attempted diff-based context injection
# against untyped markdown. It failed because the source wasn't pre-formatted.

# tomllm fixed the FORMAT. The next step: agents should inject only DELTAS to context,
# not full datum reloads.

# Current: `b00t whoami --role=domain-architect` → ~4K tokens (full AGENTS.md)
# Target:  `b00t whoami --role=domain-architect` → ~1.1K tokens (base cached + 100-token delta)

# 20% total agent cost is boilerplate headers. Delta protocol eliminates this across all roles.

## Finished State

# `.tomllm.delta` files express RFC 6902-style operations on TOML paths.
# `b00t datum patch <base> <delta>` applies delta and emits merged result.
# `b00t whoami --role=X` loads `++abstract.agent.tomllm` (base, cached) + `X.role.delta`.
# `tomllm` Rust crate gains `TomllmDelta` struct with `apply()` method.

## Delta Format

# ```toml
# X.role.delta — applies to ++abstract.agent.tomllm
[delta]
base = "_b00t_/++abstract.agent.tomllm"
version = "sha256:abc123"  # base content hash for integrity

[[delta.ops]]
op = "replace"
path = "b00t.agent.role"
value = "domain-architect"

[[delta.ops]]
op = "append"    # merge into array
path = "b00t.agent.skills"
value = "okr-routing"

[[delta.ops]]
op = "set"       # add if missing
path = "b00t.agent.tier_override"
value = "frontier"
# ```

## Ops Supported (MVP)

# | op | semantics |
# |----|-----------|
# | `replace` | overwrite scalar value at path |
# | `append` | push item to array at path |
# | `remove` | delete key at path |
# | `set` | insert key if not present, else no-op |

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `tomllm` crate: `TomllmDelta::apply(base, delta) -> Result<TomllmDoc>` with tests
# - [ ] `b00t datum patch <base.tomllm> <delta.tomllm.delta>` CLI command
# - [ ] `b00t whoami --role=executive` uses delta if `executive.role.delta` exists
# - [ ] Token count for `whoami --role=executive` drops by ≥50% vs current
# - [ ] Integrity check: delta with wrong base hash → `Err(DeltaMismatch)`

